n July 2025. Commerce.com, Inc. was founded in 2009 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christopher Travis Hess | CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $743,672 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $317K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 18%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $16K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $22K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Commerce.com, Inc. - Series 1 is a micro-cap technology business with a $274M market cap on $342M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +4.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -83% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 77% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $17M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","c